Card #5332. A stop request must reach the runtime while its turn is still
running. A real hub and a real agent-node run a fake ACP agent that holds
one turn; the stop is sent through the hub the way a user sends it. Handling
the stop only after the turn ends turns the suite red; it also checks one
cancel and one answer per stop, an honest "nothing to stop" when idle, and
that the node takes the next task afterwards.
